    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_2",
      "quote": "Although most COVID-19 cases recover without any major complications, some patients develop a progressive disease due to pneumonia and respiratory failure [6]. These patients are managed in Intensive Care Units (ICUs) and have high mortality rates, ranging between 25 and 40% [7].",
      "reason": "The Introduction describes the current state of knowledge about COVID-19 critical illness and the existing CPG landscape, including uncertainties around rapid guideline quality."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_2",
      "quote": "Given the extraordinary burden that the pandemic has created on the emergency and critical care units worldwide, there is an urgent need for evidence-based guidance to facilitate optimal clinical and policy decisionmaking.",
      "reason": "The importance and need for the review are explicitly explained, including the lack of assessment of CPGs for critically ill COVID-19 patients."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e3",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_2",
      "quote": "Four previous reviews have assessed the quality of COVID-19 CPGs [16-18]. ... However, an assessment of all the CPGs focused on the management of critically ill COVID-19 patients was lacking.",
      "reason": "Similar prior reviews are identified and cited (Zhao et al., Dagens et al., Chiesa-Estomba et al., Luo et al.), and the gap justifying the current review is explained."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e4",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "This is a review of clinical practice guidelines' methodological quality (AGREE II appraisal), not a review of intervention effects, so a mechanism of action description does not apply."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e5",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The review appraises guideline quality rather than evaluating complex interventions, so a logic model of intervention components and outcomes is not applicable."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 92
}

