  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_13b_e1",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": "We summarized the general characteristics of the CPGs with descriptive statistics. We present frequencies and proportions to summarize categorical variables used to describe the guidelines. We used mean and standard deviation (SD) to summarize the scores across all the guidelines per domain. ... We selected a cut-off for high quality CPGs of 60% or more for all the 6 AGREE II domains ... the cut-offs for low and moderate quality are < 40% and 40%-60%, respectively. For the overall quality of any CPG, whenever there was a discrepancy between OA1 and the mean score for all domains, we relied on the quality of the domain 3 score to upgrade or downgrade the overall score",
      "reason": "The Data Analysis section describes several data preparation methods: summarization with descriptive statistics, conversion of AGREE II 7-point Likert item ratings into standardized percentage domain scores (text_6), categorization of guideline quality using explicit cut-offs, assignment of healthcare system and economic classifications from external sources (Böhm et al., World Bank), a decision rule for reconciling OA1 with domain scores, and tabular presentation of extracted variables and therapeutic interventions (text_5). However, the manuscript never describes methods for handling missing data or missing summary statistics (e.g., for guidelines lacking specific extracted variables), so the data preparation methods are only partially reported."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 72
}

